-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_err_escape_newline.pcpp - Lexical: an escape before a newline

  Break step of lex_splices: of the two backslashes ending the string's
  first line the second is the splice, which joins the empty line after it;
  the first is then an escape right before a newline, and an escape never
  takes a newline, so the string is unterminated, LX0001. One mistake, two
  reports, as clang gives them: the quote that was meant to close the
  string, two lines down, now opens a string of its own that never closes
  either, a second LX0001 at that quote.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_escape_newline;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

begin
  println(/* // ERROR LX0001@39 // */ "a\\

"); // ERROR LX0001@1
end.
